        ":question/id": "03af429b-e04f-5720-9b8e-95f1a130559b",
        ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows of $A$ are $-3$, $5$, and $2$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-3+5+2=4.$",
